course: dictionary
lesson: 497
title: Looking askance
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Some words show how someone feels without saying it. Askance is one of them. «The neighbours looked askance at Toad's new motor car.» Nobody shouts or says no, but looking askance shows they doubt the car or do not approve of it.
explain: Read the clues around the word. The neighbours are looking at a car, and the sentence does not say they admire it. So askance must mean with doubt or disapproval. Swap in your meaning to check: "The neighbours looked at the car with doubt" still makes sense.
explain: The dictionary also gives an older meaning: sideways, out of the corner of your eye. Old books sometimes use it this way. In most modern stories, the meaning of doubt or disapproval is the one you need.
fact: Askance is an adverb, so it tells you how someone looks or acts.
fact: To look askance at something means to look at it with doubt, suspicion or disapproval.
fact: In old writing, «askance» can mean sideways, out of the corner of your eye.
fact: Writers choose askance to show doubt without stating it, so the reader sees the look and understands the feeling.
fact: The example sentence explains that «askance» means sideways, with doubt.
exercise: «The neighbours looked askance at Toad's new motor car.» What does looked askance show? | Falling asleep | Great delight and pride | Surprise at a loud noise | *Doubt or disapproval
exercise: Maya says askance means asked a question. What does it really mean? | Lost in the woods | Singing very loudly | Asking for help politely | *With doubt or suspicion
exercise: Which word can mean sideways, out of the corner of your eye, in old books? | Brave | *Askance | Dusty | Hurried
test: «She eyed the strange, sticky sweets askance and did not take one.» What does askance tell you about her feelings? | *She did not trust them | She loved them at once | She was angry at the shop | She was too tired to notice
test: Which sentence shows someone looking askance? | *The old man frowned and watched the stranger's bag with suspicion. | The children raced outside to play. | The baker handed out fresh buns. | The teacher smiled warmly at the new pupil.
exam: Mo reads that the crowd looked askance at the speaker. Which is the best meaning? | Ran away in fear | Happily cheered for them | *With doubt and disapproval | Fell asleep during the speech
